<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="10">
<name>Body &amp; Electrical</name>
<section id="1002Q_S000F" variety="S000F">
<name>Navigation</name>
<ttl id="1002Q_S000F_746OU_T00CJ" variety="T00CJ">
<name>HDD Navigation System</name>
<para id="RM0000002RQ05CX" category="D" type-id="3001B" name-id="NS2ZD-25" from="200912">
<name>How to Proceed with Troubleshooting</name>
<subpara id="RM0000002RQ05CX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IFV00000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<descript-diag>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Vehicle brought to workshop</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Customer Problem Analysis and Symptom Check</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Customer Problem Analysis and Symptom Check (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000014E03SX"/>)</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Check on which screen the problem symptom occurs. (Occurs on map screen only/occurs on all screens/occurs elsewhere)</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>In particular, problems related to TV images are greatly affected by the presence or absence of external factors.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Location-related factors may include power transmission lines, overhead wires, neon signs, trucks and motorcycles, vehicle radios, building conditions, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Channel (broadcast station) related factors may include radio waves that are too strong, too weak, of poor quality, unstable, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Problems during playback of CDs, DVDs, HDD, etc. are greatly affected by the presence or absence of media-related factors. Therefore, perform customer problem analysis of the problem causes according to the customer problem analysis check sheet. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000014J044X"/>)</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Basic Inspection</testtitle>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Basic Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the battery voltage.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>11 to 14 V (IG OFF)</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Inspect areas that can be checked visually, such as blown fuses, open or short circuits in the wire harness and poor connector connections.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No Abnormality</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>CAN Communication System Check</testtitle>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), select "Diagnosis" → "Vehicle Diagnosis/CAN Bus Diagnosis" → "Diagnosis Function/CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" to display the connected ECU check screen, and check all ECUs and sensors connected to CAN communication. (see <xref label="Seep10" href="RM000001R4W019X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No Abnormality</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Abnormal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>   Go to CAN Communication System (<xref label="Seep11" href="RM000001R4W019X"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Check Power Supply to Navigation Receiver Assembly</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Navigation Receiver Assembly Power Supply Check</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn ACC ON.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Check that the initial screen is displayed on the display of the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If "Screen Off" is set, cancel it.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No Abnormality</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Initial screen is not displayed</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to Problem Symptoms Table: Screen remains black when ACC ON (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM0000008WW03VX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the procedure, see <xref label="Seep04" href="RM000000OCQ05TX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check DTC</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Record the DTCs.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear DTC</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Recheck DTC</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Based on the recorded DTCs, reproduce the problem symptom and check whether the DTCs are output again.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The navigation receiver assembly outputs DTCs for the following systems. If a DTC not listed in the HDD navigation system - Diagnostic Trouble Code Chart is output, refer to the other system.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>System Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Reference</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Back Guide Monitor System</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep05" href="RM0000002O403WX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>ETC System</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep12" href="RM000001US9017X"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No code, symptom can be confirmed and reproduced</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No code, symptom cannot be confirmed and reproduced</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Code output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to Symptom Simulation (see <xref label="Seep06" href="RM000000ABY07EX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result>C</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 9</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>List by Symptom</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Problem Symptoms Table (see <xref label="Seep07" href="RM0000008WW03VX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Not listed in List by Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Corresponds to List by Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 9</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Perform troubleshooting using the following methods based on the problem symptom</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Diagnosis System (see <xref label="Seep08" href="RM0000002RV04DX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Terminals of ECU (see <xref label="Seep09" href="RM0000002RT04XX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Adjust, Repair or Replace</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Work after Replacement</testtitle>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Depending on the part replaced, setting work may be necessary. (see <xref label="Seep13" href="RM0000002RM03SX"/>)</ptxt>
</atten4>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Confirmation Test</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
<action-ci-fin>END</action-ci-fin>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
</descript-diag>
</content5>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>